[0m[0m
Verification method was differential testing against [38;5;10mgcc -O2[0m on the original [38;5;10mmain.c[0m (built into [38;5;10m/tmp/cref[0m, since [38;5;10mc_src/[0m is read-only), comparing [38;5;10mod -c[0m of stdout: 35 hand-picked edge cases, 16 re-runs of negative/NUL cases after I noticed bash [38;5;10mprintf[0m was swallowing [38;5;10m-4[0m as a flag and silently feeding empty stdin, 8 perl-driven cases for genuine NUL bytes, and 400 randomized inputs. Zero mismatches.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The parts that needed care:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mstrtol[0m is emulated by hand rather than delegated to Rust's [38;5;10mstr::parse[0m, because the C accepts trailing garbage ([38;5;10m12abc[0m → 12) and leading whitespace/sign, and distinguishes "no conversion" ([38;5;10mendp == str[0m) from a successful parse of 0. I model [38;5;10mendp[0m as an offset where [38;5;10m0[0m means no conversion, and track ERANGE separately so that out-of-[38;5;10mlong[0m values fail the [38;5;10merrno == 0[0m check while merely out-of-[38;5;10mint[0m values fail the range check — two distinct rejection paths in the original, both reachable.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mfgets[0m reads byte-at-a-time, stopping after a newline or at 99 bytes, and the result is truncated at the first embedded NUL to mirror the C buffer's string semantics. On immediate EOF the C buffer keeps its initial [38;5;10m""[0m, which is the same empty result.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mfloors++[0m and [38;5;10mbedrooms +=[0m use [38;5;10mwrapping_add[0m. Signed overflow is UB in C, but I reproduced the observed x86-64 wrapping behavior rather than panicking, per the no-bug-fixing requirement — confirmed against inputs like [38;5;10m2147483000[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
One thing I could not fully verify: [38;5;10m%.1f[0m and Rust's [38;5;10m{:.1}[0m can disagree on exact ties under some rounding paths. It does not arise here because [38;5;10mbathrooms[0m starts at 2.5 and only ever has [38;5;10m1.0[0m added, so it stays an exact half and needs no rounding. My [38;5;10mformat_f1[0m also handles nan/inf glibc-style, which is unreachable in this program but harmless.[0m[0m
